    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: net/sched: ets: Always remove class from active list before deleting in ets_qdisc_change (CVE-2025-71066)\n\n* kernel: HID: wacom: fix out-of-bounds read in wacom_intuos_bt_irq (CVE-2026-43051)\n\n* kernel: procfs: fix missing RCU protection when reading real_parent in do_task_stat() (CVE-2026-46259)\n\n* kernel: dm cache policy smq: fix missing locks in invalidating cache blocks (CVE-2026-53062)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: hci_ldisc: Clear HCI_UART_PROTO_INIT on error (CVE-2026-53073)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: synproxy: refresh tcphdr after skb_ensure_writable (CVE-2026-64007)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-tcp: check INIT_FAILED before nvmet_req_uninit in digest error path (CVE-2026-64534)\n\n* kernel: scsi: libiscsi_tcp: Bound SCSI Response data segment to the connection buffer (CVE-2026-74556)\n\n* kernel: nvme-tcp: fix host memory disclosure on R2T for a read command (CVE-2026-89481)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (CVE-2026-98432)\n\n* kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* The Kernel panic occurred at strlen+0x0 because a race event filter treats the user space pointer as a normal pointer (JIRA:RHEL-291138)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
